'' =================================================================================================
''
''   File....... test_bench_t0.spin2
''   Purpose.... Tier 0 bench harness -- ten driver-audit findings provable with no motor,
''               no motion and no risk (DOCs/analyses/BENCH-TEST-PLAN-2026-09-10.md Section 3),
''               extended with T0-11..T0-15 sign-off cells (task 3504, design
''               DOCs/plans/VISIT-SIGNOFF-DESIGN.md SS H.1)
''   Authors.... Stephen M Moraco
''               -- Copyright (c) 2026 Iron Sheep Productions, LLC
''               -- see below for terms of use
''   E-mail..... stephen@ironsheep.biz
''   Started.... 10 Sep 2026
''   Updated.... 13 Sep 2026 -- task 3504: T0-11..T0-15 sign-off cells (SIGNOFF-DECL/SIGNOFF
''               records, design SS B.4), reordered so T0-11/T0-13 precede T0-10 and T0-15b
''               (cog exhaustion) runs last, T0-12 hand-rotation anchor split out under
''               -D T0_HAND, and PL-23's remaining T0 booleans (T0-3 agree, T0-4 legal) fixed
''               to print TRUE/FALSE.
''               14 Sep 2026 -- task 3537 T0 BOOL: R4-T0-1M-TICKS, R1-T0-START, R1-T0-RESTART and
''               R1-T0-EXHAUST are BOOL cells (measured TRUE/FALSE = every condition ANDed), so
''               no record can print an in-band number beside a FAIL.
''               14 Sep 2026 -- task 3537 T0 follow-ups: SF_RESTART_HI / SF_EXHAUST_HI removed (unused
''               since the BOOL change), and every sign-off cell prints NOMEAS,n,0 when a trapped
''               call it judges aborted (design SS H.1), found by a completion flag, not the trap's
''               value -- R4-T0-1M-TICKS, R1-T0-START/RESTART/EXHAUST, R8-T0-ZXS, R3-T0-STOPPED,
''               R2-T0-REPEAT/DIRTY/EMPTY and R10-T0-STOPREADY.
''
'' =================================================================================================

{ Rig: the dual 6.5" platform -- two Rev B boards, 18.5V pack.

  BUILD WITH -D BENCH_CFG. That selects isp_bldc_motor_userconfig_bench.spin2,
  a peer config file stating the bench and nothing else, in place of
  isp_bldc_motor_userconfig.spin2. Nobody has to activate a block, and the
  file end users edit is neither read nor written by a bench run:

      pnut-ts -l -d -D BENCH_CFG test_bench_t0.spin2

  It still compiles without the flag -- build-check.sh does exactly that --
  against whichever user block is active. Under a block with
  WHEEL_DIA_IN_INCH = 0.0 the T0-3 and T0-6 distance conversions correctly
  report themselves unavailable rather than returning a tick count.

  Every test below calls testSetup(), which runs the whole of init() -- board
  detection, constant derivation, power tables, unit conversion -- WITHOUT
  starting a driver cog, so the motor rail can stay off and the motor can stay
  unplugged. The exceptions are T0-10 (needs a real, running driver cog so the
  fourth ADC channel is actively calibrated and frame-locked; it still
  commands zero speed, so nothing turns), T0-11 (five real start()/stop()
  cycles reading live telemetry at zero command), T0-13 (a real start() held
  at zero command for 1000 ms), T0-14b (a real start()/stop() cycle to prove
  the post-stop board-type read stays clean) and T0-15 (start()/stop() cycles
  probing cog accounting). Keep the motor rail on for all of these; none of
  them ever commands nonzero speed.

  Output: one tagged line per data point, "T0-n,field,value,...", on the plain
  debug stream. Sign-off records ("SIGNOFF-DECL,..." / "SIGNOFF,...") are a
  second, separately-tagged stream consumed by tools/signoff-collate.py (task
  3537 phase 2; design DOCs/plans/VISIT-SIGNOFF-DESIGN.md). Every call this
  harness makes into a method that can abort() (per an audit of
  isp_bldc_motor.spin2's `abort` sites against every motor.*/motorA.*/motorB.*
  call below) is \-trapped so an abort can never crash this harness and take
  the rest of the suite down with it -- see the per-test comments for how to
  read each, since the trapped return value alone cannot distinguish "the
  call finished and returned zero" from "the call aborted with no value" when
  no driver cog is running. No sign-off cell relies on that value: every
  trapped call a verdict depends on goes through the startTrapped()/
  setupTrapped()/stopDistanceTrapped() completion-flag wrappers (see
  VAR { abort-trap completion flag }), and a cell instance whose call aborted
  prints NOMEAS,n,0 rather than a PASS or FAIL. Ground truth is the object's own pre-existing
  "! ERROR:" / "*???*" debug() line, which fires immediately before every
  abort site this harness exercises and appears in the same capture right
  after this harness's own tag. As a second line of defense, main() also
  \-traps each testT0_n() call itself, so even an abort site this audit
  missed cannot stop the suite short -- a test that goes silent after its own
  "begin" tag but before its "end" tag is the sign of exactly that. Per
  design rule 3 (SS 0), every declared sign-off cell still gets a verdict on
  that path: a test whose call aborted and skipped its own emitSignoff-style
  code prints NOMEAS,n,0 from the enclosing test method wherever that is
  reachable; where the abort happens inside main()'s own outer trap (a test
  method going silent entirely) no further SIGNOFF for that cell is
  possible from here -- the design's own rule 3 note (a declared cell with no
  verdict is NOMEAS by the host's convention, reason NOT_REACHED).

  T0-1's six derived constants (dead_gap, pwm_limit, duty_min, duty_max,
  adc_fram, frame_cnt) and T0-3 (finding F) both read via two new TEST-USE
  ONLY getters on isp_bldc_motor.spin2: testGetDriveConstants() and
  testGetStopHallTicks(). Both are pure read-only snapshots.

  If anything behaves unexpectedly during T0-10/T0-11/T0-13/T0-14b/T0-15 (the
  tests with the rail on): physical battery disconnect, not
  emergencyCutoff() -- it self-cancels in about 250 ms (finding S-4).

  T0-12 (hand-rotation anchor) is deliberately NOT part of this unattended
  run. It is compiled in only under -D T0_HAND, has its own bench-run.sh tier
  (t0-hand), waits on an operator keypress rather than a timer, and carries
  no sign-off cell.
}

CON { bench target }

' Which motor this harness talks to. Deliberately NOT read from the user
' config: a dual-motor block defines LEFT_MOTOR_BASE and RIGHT_MOTOR_BASE and
' no ONLY_MOTOR_BASE at all, so reading that user constant will not COMPILE on
' a dual bench -- which is what the real bench is (dual 6.5" wheels, Rev B
' boards, 18.5V pack). PINS_P16_P31 is a real motor under every config block
' in isp_bldc_motor_userconfig.spin2: the right wheel on the dual 6.5"/18.5V
' block, the left wheel on the alternate dual block, and the sole motor on
' every single-motor block. Everything else -- motor type, drive voltage,
' wheel diameter -- still comes from whichever block is active, so the harness
' describes the hardware the operator says is connected.
    T0_MOTOR_BASE = motor.PINS_P16_P31

' Second populated base for T0-14's board-detection sweeps (R2-T0-REPEAT,
' R2-T0-DIRTY). PINS_P32_P47 is a legal enum value under every config block
' regardless of which is active, so this compiles everywhere; it is only
' actually wired to a second board on the dual-motor bench. Using the raw
' PINS_* enum (not user.LEFT_MOTOR_BASE) sidesteps the same single-motor
' compile hazard T0_MOTOR_BASE's comment above describes.
    T0_SECOND_BASE = motor.PINS_P32_P47

CON { timing }

    CLK_FREQ = 270_000_000                                      ' matches the audit's worked dead_gap example
    _clkfreq = CLK_FREQ

CON { cog-exhaustion probe (T0-8, T0-15) }

    MAX_SPACER_COGS   = 7                                       ' every cog besides this harness's own
    SPACER_STACK_LONGS = 32                                     ' generous headroom for a trivial idle loop

CON { hand-rotation anchor (T0-12, -D T0_HAND only) }

    T0_12_HALL_OFFSET = 5                                       ' pin_hall_u is base+5; hall inputs are base+5..base+7
    T0_12_HALL_SPAN   = 2                                       ' addpins operand: three hall pins
    T0_12_POLL_MS     = 1                                       ' hall poll period while counting
    T0_12_KEY_POLLS   = 100                                     ' polls between keypress checks (~100 ms)
    T0_12_PRINT_POLLS = 500                                     ' polls between progress lines (~500 ms)
    T0_12_KEY_WAIT_MS = 50                                      ' keypress poll period before counting starts

CON { sign-off limits (task 3504) -- compiled-in CON limits per cell, each with its provenance;
      full derivations in DOCs/plans/VISIT-SIGNOFF-DESIGN.md SS A.4/A.5 }

    SF_ZXS_LO     = 0            ' definitional -- a max - min spread cannot be negative
    SF_ZXS_HI     = 50           ' DERIVED -- SS A.5-e: 2x the predicted post-fix spread (~2.5 mV), in MV_X10

    SF_STOP_LO    = 0
    SF_STOP_HI    = 0            ' DERIVED -- stationary halls never transition (SS A.4 row 3)

    SF_REPEAT_LO  = 0
    SF_REPEAT_HI  = 0            ' DERIVED -- every one of 32 reads on a real board must read REV_B

    SF_TICKS_LO   = 173
    SF_TICKS_HI   = 174          ' DERIVED -- SS A.5-b: 1000 mm x 90 / 518.6 mm = 173.5, truncated or rounded

    SF_COG_LO     = 0
    SF_COG_HI     = 7            ' DERIVED -- start() returns a cog id 0..7 on success (isp_bldc_motor.spin2:86)

    SF_RESTART_LO = 0            ' DERIVED -- PL-24 fix: a second start() must orphan no cog

    SF_EXHAUST_LO = -1           ' DERIVED -- coginit()'s documented -1-on-failure form (isp_bldc_motor.spin2:110-113)

OBJ { objects under test }

#ifdef BENCH_CFG
    user    : "isp_bldc_motor_userconfig_bench"                 ' bench compile-time hardware config (-D BENCH_CFG)
#else
    user    : "isp_bldc_motor_userconfig"                       ' active compile-time hardware config
#endif
    motor   : "isp_bldc_motor"                                  ' primary instance, T0-1/2/3/4/5/6/8/10/11/13/14/15
    motorA  : "isp_bldc_motor"                                  ' second instance, T0-7 overlap probe and T0-14b scratch
    motorB  : "isp_bldc_motor"                                  ' second instance, T0-7 overlap probe only

VAR { cog-exhaustion probe stacks (T0-8, T0-15) }

    LONG    spacerStacks[MAX_SPACER_COGS * SPACER_STACK_LONGS]

VAR { abort-trap completion flag (T0-3, T0-11, T0-13, T0-14a/b/c, T0-15a/b/c/d) }

' How an aborted call is told apart from a normal return, for every sign-off cell whose
' verdict depends on a \-trapped call (design SS H.1: an aborted call prints NOMEAS,n,0, never
' PASS or FAIL): R4-T0-1M-TICKS, R1-T0-START, R1-T0-RESTART, R1-T0-EXHAUST, R8-T0-ZXS,
' R3-T0-STOPPED, R2-T0-REPEAT, R2-T0-DIRTY, R2-T0-EMPTY and R10-T0-STOPREADY.
'
' NOT the trapped value. Every abort these calls can reach is a bare `abort` with no value,
' which "returns 0 to the trapping caller" (p2kbSpin2Abort): start() -> startEx() -> init()
' and testSetup() -> init() (isp_bldc_motor.spin2:105, :170) reach validatePinBase() (:259, via
' :272), confgurePowerLimits() (:1376, :1408, :1422, via :399) and motorVoltage() (:1455, via
' :1427); stopAfterDistance() aborts at :606, :610, :632. start() legitimately RETURNS a cog id
' 0..7 or -1 (:86, :112, :121), so neither 0 nor -1 can mean "aborted" -- and a 0 would even
' pass a `startResult >= 0` test as a cog id.
' NOT a sentinel pre-loaded into the result: `x := \call()` assigns whatever the trap
' delivers on both paths, so the pre-load is overwritten either way.
'
' CHOSEN: a completion flag, the pattern test_bench_char.spin2 already uses
' (brakeStartTrapped()/brakeStartCall() :2240-2265, steerStartTrapped()/steerStartCall()
' :1949-1969). xxxTrapped() sets bTrapPending TRUE, then calls \xxxCall(); xxxCall() makes the
' library call and clears bTrapPending on the very next line. When an ABORT executes, "stack
' frames are unwound (popped) until a trap is found", and the statement after it is "Never
' executed" (p2kbSpin2Abort) -- the same fact main()'s own \testT0_n() backstop rests on -- so
' that line runs only when the library call returned. bTrapPending still TRUE after the trap
' is therefore reachable ONLY by an abort. Cog 0 only; the spacer cogs never touch it.

    LONG    bTrapPending

' R10-T0-STOPREADY (T0-15d) judges the state T0-15c's own stop() left behind, so it is valid
' only when T0-15c ran to that stop() with neither of its start()s aborted AND both returned a
' cog id. A start() that returns -1 normally also calls stop() (the PL-36 failure branch), which
' leaves DCS_Unknown with no driver ever run -- a PASS read from nothing. T0-15c clears this
' first and sets it last, so a T0-15c cut short by any abort also leaves it FALSE.
    LONG    bRestartStopValid

PUB main() | trapResult
'' Run every Tier 0 test in sequence and tag its result on the debug stream.
'' Every test's own abort-capable calls are individually \-trapped (see the
'' per-test comments); this loop also \-traps each testT0_n() call itself as
'' a backstop, so a single test failing -- whether from a trapped call this
'' harness reports on, or from an abort site the per-test trapping missed --
'' can never stop the rest of the suite from running or keep DONE from
'' printing. The very last thing printed, alone on its own line with nothing
'' else in that debug() call, is the literal text DEBUG_END_SESSION --
'' tools/bench-run.sh runs pnut-term-ts with --exit-on-end-session, and that
'' phrase is its end-of-session marker. Emitting it here, only after DONE,
'' lets that batch mode close the terminal itself once the suite has
'' genuinely finished, instead of waiting on an operator keypress or a fixed
'' timeout. No other debug() output anywhere in this harness may contain
'' this phrase, or the session would end early.
''

' @local trapResult - discarded; testT0_n() returns nothing meaningful, this
'                      exists only so \testT0_n() has somewhere to land

    debug("* test_bench_t0 -- Tier 0: no motor, no motion, no risk (T0-10/11/13/14b/15 excepted)")
    debug("* active config: motor_type_enum=", udec_(user.MOTOR_TYPE), " base=", udec_(T0_MOTOR_BASE), " voltage_enum=", udec_(user.DRIVE_VOLTAGE), " wheel_dia_x10=", udec_(round(user.WHEEL_DIA_IN_INCH *. 10.0)))
    debug("* bench expects MOTOR_TYPE=MOTR_6_5_INCH (0) and wheel_dia_x10=65; with wheel_dia_x10=0 the T0-3/T0-6 distance conversions report unavailable rather than a tick count")

#ifdef T0_HAND
    ' T0_HAND build (bench-run.sh t0-hand): T0-12 only. It is an operator-attended reference
    ' measurement with no sign-off cell, so this build runs none of the unattended tests and
    ' declares no cells -- its log can never be mistaken for an unattended Tier 0 run.
    trapResult := \testT0_12()
#else
    ' Sign-off declarations (design rule 3, SS 0): one per cell this binary will judge, emitted
    ' before anything starts a cog. Row 8 (R8-T0-ZXS) covers all four channel variants (ZXS_I/
    ' U/V/W) under a single declared cell, per design SS A.2's "feature row is the set of cells
    ' sharing row" -- the manifest joins on the cell id, not the per-channel crit token.
    debug("SIGNOFF-DECL,sf,1,bin,T0,cell,R8-T0-ZXS,task,3529")
    debug("SIGNOFF-DECL,sf,1,bin,T0,cell,R3-T0-STOPPED,task,3501")
    debug("SIGNOFF-DECL,sf,1,bin,T0,cell,R2-T0-REPEAT,task,3500")
    debug("SIGNOFF-DECL,sf,1,bin,T0,cell,R2-T0-DIRTY,task,3500")
    debug("SIGNOFF-DECL,sf,1,bin,T0,cell,R2-T0-EMPTY,task,3500")
    debug("SIGNOFF-DECL,sf,1,bin,T0,cell,R4-T0-1M-TICKS,task,3502")
    debug("SIGNOFF-DECL,sf,1,bin,T0,cell,R1-T0-START,task,3499")
    debug("SIGNOFF-DECL,sf,1,bin,T0,cell,R1-T0-RESTART,task,3499")
    debug("SIGNOFF-DECL,sf,1,bin,T0,cell,R10-T0-STOPREADY,task,3533")
    debug("SIGNOFF-DECL,sf,1,bin,T0,cell,R1-T0-EXHAUST,task,3499")

    trapResult := \testT0_1()
    trapResult := \testT0_2()
    trapResult := \testT0_3()
    trapResult := \testT0_4()
    trapResult := \testT0_5()
    trapResult := \testT0_6()
    trapResult := \testT0_7()

    ' T0-11 and T0-13 run BEFORE T0-10 (design SS H.1 order rule): both are real start()/stop()
    ' cycles on `motor`, and running them before T0-10's own start()/stop() (and well before
    ' T0-8's destructive cog exhaustion) keeps every one of their five/one start()s clean.
    trapResult := \testT0_11()
    trapResult := \testT0_13()

    ' T0-14 (board-detection sweeps) also belongs on the non-destructive side of T0-8, and after
    ' T0-7 so it can release T0-7's motorA/motorB pin claims itself (each sub-test does so).
    trapResult := \testT0_14a()
    trapResult := \testT0_14b()
    trapResult := \testT0_14c()

    ' T0-15a/c/d (start/restart/stopready) are non-destructive cog accounting; T0-15b
    ' (exhaustion) is deliberately last, after T0-8's slot (see T0-8's own comment).
    trapResult := \testT0_15a()
    trapResult := \testT0_15c()
    trapResult := \testT0_15d()

    ' T0-10 runs BEFORE T0-8 deliberately. Both drive the same motor object,
    ' and T0-8 is the destructive one: it occupies every spare cog so that
    ' start() must fail, which leaves the object half-initialised. Run in the
    ' other order, T0-10's own start() then returns 0 and its ADC reading is
    ' never taken -- observed in the 2026-09-10 bench run. Destructive tests
    ' go last.
    trapResult := \testT0_10()
    trapResult := \testT0_8()

    ' R1-T0-EXHAUST (T0-15b) runs last of all, after T0-8's slot, per design SS H.1: it is its
    ' own, harsher cog-exhaustion probe (a real start() under exhaustion, not T0-8's) and must
    ' never leave fewer free cogs than it found, so nothing after it can rely on a spare cog.
    trapResult := \testT0_15b()
#endif

    debug("* test_bench_t0 -- DONE")
    debug("DEBUG_END_SESSION")

PRI testT0_1() | eBoardRev, rSenseOhms, pBoardStr, deadGap, pwmLimit, dutyMin, dutyMax, adcFrame, frameCnt, trappedResult
' A1 / A3: run the whole of init() through testSetup() and read back what is
' publicly readable, plus the six derived drive constants via the new
' testGetDriveConstants() getter. A1's criterion is dead_gap == 70 (not 14)
' at 270 MHz -- see this test's tagged "consts" line. testSetup() reaches
' confgurePowerLimits() (via init()), which aborts if user.DRIVE_VOLTAGE is
' not legal for user.MOTOR_TYPE, so it is \-trapped; every field it sets
' before that point (pinbase, eDetectedBoard, the six drive constants) is
' already valid by the time confgurePowerLimits() runs, so a trapped abort
' here does not invalidate the rest of this test's readback.
'
' @local eBoardRev - value returned by getBoardType() after testSetup()
' @local rSenseOhms - F_REV_A_RSENSE or F_REV_B_RSENSE for the detected board
' @local pBoardStr - pointer to boardIdString()'s result
' @local deadGap - dead_gap, expect 70 at 270 MHz (A1); 14 means STOP, re-read at a second clock
' @local pwmLimit - pwm_limit, the PWM duty hard limit derived from dead_gap
' @local dutyMin - duty_min, minimum PWM duty cycle
' @local dutyMax - duty_max, maximum PWM duty cycle
' @local adcFrame - adc_fram, ADC sample period matching the PWM frame width
' @local frameCnt - frame_cnt, clock-ticks for one PWM_RATE_IN_HZ period
' @local trappedResult - testSetup()'s trapped return value (0 is ambiguous, see header)

    debug("T0-1,begin,clkfreq,", udec_(CLKFREQ))
    trappedResult := \motor.testSetup(T0_MOTOR_BASE, user.DRIVE_VOLTAGE, motor.BRD_AUTO_DET)
    debug("T0-1,testsetup,trapped_result,", sdec_(trappedResult))
    eBoardRev := motor.getBoardType()
    pBoardStr := motor.boardIdString()
    rSenseOhms := (eBoardRev == motor.REV_B) ? motor.F_REV_B_RSENSE : motor.F_REV_A_RSENSE
    deadGap, pwmLimit, dutyMin, dutyMax, adcFrame, frameCnt := motor.testGetDriveConstants()
    debug("T0-1,consts,dead_gap,", udec_(deadGap), ",pwm_limit,", udec_(pwmLimit), ",duty_min,", udec_(dutyMin), ",duty_max,", udec_(dutyMax), ",adc_fram,", udec_(adcFrame), ",frame_cnt,", udec_(frameCnt))
    debug("T0-1,end,detected_board,", udec_(eBoardRev), ",rsense,", udec_(rSenseOhms), ",boardstring,", zstr_(pBoardStr))

PRI testT0_2() | eBoardRev, pBoardStr, trappedResult
' A2 / A3: force BRD_REV_A on a board that auto-detects Rev B. bUserForced has
' no getter, but getInternalDetectMode() sets it TRUE unconditionally whenever
' the caller passes BRD_REV_A/BRD_REV_B -- true by construction for this call.
' boardIdString() carries the empirical half: it embeds "-USER FORCED" only
' when bUserForced was actually set, so the returned text is A3's evidence,
' not a recomputation of it. testSetup() is \-trapped for the same reason as
' T0-1 -- confgurePowerLimits() (reached via init()) aborts on an illegal
' user.DRIVE_VOLTAGE / user.MOTOR_TYPE pairing, and the board-detect fields
' this test reads are set before that point regardless.
'
' @local eBoardRev - value returned by getBoardType() after the forced testSetup()
' @local pBoardStr - pointer to boardIdString()'s result
' @local trappedResult - testSetup()'s trapped return value (0 is ambiguous, see header)

    debug("T0-2,begin,requested,BRD_REV_A")
    trappedResult := \motor.testSetup(T0_MOTOR_BASE, user.DRIVE_VOLTAGE, motor.BRD_REV_A)
    debug("T0-2,testsetup,trapped_result,", sdec_(trappedResult))
    eBoardRev := motor.getBoardType()
    pBoardStr := motor.boardIdString()
    debug("T0-2,end,detected_board,", udec_(eBoardRev), ",expect_forced,TRUE,boardstring,", zstr_(pBoardStr))

PRI testT0_3() | ticksM, ticksCm, ticksMm, trappedM, trappedCm, trappedMm, bAbortM, bAbortCm, bAbortMm, bAgree, bTicksInBand, bPass
' F: stopAfterDistance() computes its tick target in three equivalent ways --
' 1 DDU_M, 100 DDU_CM, 1000 DDU_MM -- and stores it in the private VAR
' motorStopHallTicks, read back here via the new testGetStopHallTicks()
' getter. All three should agree; DDU_M coming out a factor of ten short of
' the other two CONFIRMS finding F. stopAfterDistance() also aborts outright
' when user.WHEEL_DIA_IN_INCH is 0.0 (unknown wheel diameter) -- the exact
' failure that killed the whole T0 suite on the 2026-09-10 bench run, since
' the active config at the time had WHEEL_DIA_IN_INCH = 0.0 and this call was
' not trapped. All three calls are now \-trapped, matching the T0-4/T0-6
' pattern, so an abort here can never stop T0-4..T0-10 from running. As with
' those two, the trapped result alone cannot distinguish "completed, ticks
' still 0" from "aborted with no value" -- ground truth is the object's own
' "! ERROR:" debug() line, which appears in the same capture right after each
' tag below when the call actually aborted.
'
' task 3504 / R4-T0-1M-TICKS: a BOOL cell (task 3537). measured is TRUE only when
' the DDU_M reading (ticksM) is in SF_TICKS_LO..SF_TICKS_HI (SS A.5-b) AND the
' three units agree, since agreement is required for any of them to be trusted.
' The three raw tick targets are printed on the T0-3 ddu_* lines above it.
' The cell judges all three calls, so it is NOMEAS,n,0 when ANY of them aborted
' (design SS H.1) -- found by stopDistanceTrapped()'s completion flag, never by the
' trapped value (see VAR { abort-trap completion flag }). Each ddu_* line says
' whether its own call aborted.
'
' @local ticksM - motorStopHallTicks after stopAfterDistance(1, DDU_M)
' @local ticksCm - motorStopHallTicks after stopAfterDistance(100, DDU_CM)
' @local ticksMm - motorStopHallTicks after stopAfterDistance(1000, DDU_MM)
' @local trappedM - stopAfterDistance(1, DDU_M)'s trapped return value
' @local trappedCm - stopAfterDistance(100, DDU_CM)'s trapped return value
' @local trappedMm - stopAfterDistance(1000, DDU_MM)'s trapped return value
' @local bAbortM - TRUE only when stopAfterDistance(1, DDU_M) aborted
' @local bAbortCm - TRUE only when stopAfterDistance(100, DDU_CM) aborted
' @local bAbortMm - TRUE only when stopAfterDistance(1000, DDU_MM) aborted
' @local bAgree - TRUE when all three tick readings match (PL-23: printed as TRUE/FALSE)
' @local bTicksInBand - TRUE when ticksM falls in SF_TICKS_LO..SF_TICKS_HI
' @local bPass - bAgree and bTicksInBand, this cell's measured value and verdict

    debug("T0-3,begin")

    trappedM, bAbortM := stopDistanceTrapped(1, motor.DDU_M)
    ticksM := motor.testGetStopHallTicks()
    debug("T0-3,ddu_m,1,trapped_result,", sdec_(trappedM), ",ticks,", udec_(ticksM), ",aborted,", zstr_(bAbortM ? @"TRUE" : @"FALSE"))

    trappedCm, bAbortCm := stopDistanceTrapped(100, motor.DDU_CM)
    ticksCm := motor.testGetStopHallTicks()
    debug("T0-3,ddu_cm,100,trapped_result,", sdec_(trappedCm), ",ticks,", udec_(ticksCm), ",aborted,", zstr_(bAbortCm ? @"TRUE" : @"FALSE"))

    trappedMm, bAbortMm := stopDistanceTrapped(1000, motor.DDU_MM)
    ticksMm := motor.testGetStopHallTicks()
    debug("T0-3,ddu_mm,1000,trapped_result,", sdec_(trappedMm), ",ticks,", udec_(ticksMm), ",aborted,", zstr_(bAbortMm ? @"TRUE" : @"FALSE"))

    bAgree := (ticksM == ticksCm) and (ticksCm == ticksMm)
    debug("T0-3,end,agree,", zstr_(bAgree ? @"TRUE" : @"FALSE"))

    bTicksInBand := (ticksM >= SF_TICKS_LO) and (ticksM <= SF_TICKS_HI)
    bPass := bAgree and bTicksInBand
    if bAbortM or bAbortCm or bAbortMm
        debug("SIGNOFF,sf,1,bin,T0,cell,R4-T0-1M-TICKS,task,3502,motor,NONE,crit,DDU_M_TICKS,measured,NA,lo,TRUE,hi,TRUE,units,BOOL,n,0,verdict,NOMEAS")
    else
        debug("SIGNOFF,sf,1,bin,T0,cell,R4-T0-1M-TICKS,task,3502,motor,NONE,crit,DDU_M_TICKS,measured,", zstr_(bPass ? @"TRUE" : @"FALSE"), ",lo,TRUE,hi,TRUE,units,BOOL,n,1,verdict,", zstr_(bPass ? @"PASS" : @"FAIL"))

PRI testT0_4() | pwrEnum, legalVolt, trappedResult
' O: validVoltageForChoice() never aborts, so the full PWR_* sweep is safe.
' testSetup()/init() take an eMotorVoltage parameter but never read it -- the
' voltage that actually reaches confgurePowerLimits() is always the
' compile-time user.DRIVE_VOLTAGE (a distinct finding from O, noted in the
' dispatch report). So only the ACTIVE config's voltage can be exercised
' through testSetup() in any one build; confirming O specifically for
' PWR_25p9V needs a rebuild with DRIVE_VOLTAGE = PWR_25p9V. Either way the
' \-trapped call below cannot crash this harness.
'
' @local pwrEnum - PWR_* value under test, PWR_6p0V..PWR_25p9V
' @local legalVolt - validVoltageForChoice()'s return for pwrEnum
' @local trappedResult - testSetup()'s trapped return value (see note above)

    repeat pwrEnum from motor.PWR_6p0V to motor.PWR_25p9V
        legalVolt := motor.validVoltageForChoice(pwrEnum)
        debug("T0-4,validate,pwr_enum,", udec_(pwrEnum), ",legal,", zstr_((legalVolt <> motor.INVALID_VOLTAGE) ? @"TRUE" : @"FALSE"))

    debug("T0-4,testsetup,begin,active_drive_voltage_enum,", udec_(user.DRIVE_VOLTAGE))
    trappedResult := \motor.testSetup(T0_MOTOR_BASE, user.DRIVE_VOLTAGE, motor.BRD_AUTO_DET)
    debug("T0-4,testsetup,end,trapped_result,", sdec_(trappedResult), ",note,zero_is_ambiguous_see_library_ERROR_line")

PRI testT0_5() | minRamp, maxRamp, incRamp, decrRamp
' G: setAcceleration() writes {rate} straight into ramp_inc with no
' validation. Sweep 0, -1, 1, 10_000_000 and read back via getRampingValues().
'
' @local minRamp - ramp_min read back after each setAcceleration() call
' @local maxRamp - ramp_max read back after each setAcceleration() call
' @local incRamp - ramp_inc read back after each setAcceleration() call
' @local decrRamp - ramp_down read back after each setAcceleration() call

    motor.setAcceleration(0)
    minRamp, maxRamp, incRamp, decrRamp := motor.getRampingValues()
    debug("T0-5,accel,0,ramp_min,", sdec_(minRamp), ",ramp_max,", sdec_(maxRamp), ",ramp_inc,", sdec_(incRamp), ",ramp_down,", sdec_(decrRamp))

    motor.setAcceleration(-1)
    minRamp, maxRamp, incRamp, decrRamp := motor.getRampingValues()
    debug("T0-5,accel,-1,ramp_min,", sdec_(minRamp), ",ramp_max,", sdec_(maxRamp), ",ramp_inc,", sdec_(incRamp), ",ramp_down,", sdec_(decrRamp))

    motor.setAcceleration(1)
    minRamp, maxRamp, incRamp, decrRamp := motor.getRampingValues()
    debug("T0-5,accel,1,ramp_min,", sdec_(minRamp), ",ramp_max,", sdec_(maxRamp), ",ramp_inc,", sdec_(incRamp), ",ramp_down,", sdec_(decrRamp))

    motor.setAcceleration(10_000_000)
    minRamp, maxRamp, incRamp, decrRamp := motor.getRampingValues()
    debug("T0-5,accel,10000000,ramp_min,", sdec_(minRamp), ",ramp_max,", sdec_(maxRamp), ",ramp_inc,", sdec_(incRamp), ",ramp_down,", sdec_(decrRamp))

PRI testT0_6() | trappedResult
' I/T, K: getDistance(DDU_KM)/(DDU_MI) are valid units and are not expected to
' abort -- read straight off the trapped result. getRotationCount(99) and
' stopAfterDistance(0, DDU_IN) are deliberately invalid/out-of-range and DO
' abort in the current code. All four calls are \-trapped so an actual abort
' can never crash this harness. Tier 0 has no motion, so every one of these
' methods' non-abort return is also 0 (posTrkHallTicks never advances without
' a running driver) -- the trapped result alone cannot distinguish "completed,
' returned 0" from "aborted with no value" for any of the four. Ground truth
' is the object's own "! ERROR:" debug() line, already emitted immediately
' before each abort site, visible in the same capture right after this tag.
'
' @local trappedResult - the trapped call's return value (see note above)

    trappedResult := \motor.getDistance(motor.DDU_KM)
    debug("T0-6,call,getDistance_KM,trapped_result,", sdec_(trappedResult))

    trappedResult := \motor.getDistance(motor.DDU_MI)
    debug("T0-6,call,getDistance_MI,trapped_result,", sdec_(trappedResult))

    trappedResult := \motor.getRotationCount(99)
    debug("T0-6,call,getRotationCount_99,trapped_result,", sdec_(trappedResult))

    trappedResult := \motor.stopAfterDistance(0, motor.DDU_IN)
    debug("T0-6,call,stopAfterDistance_0in,trapped_result,", sdec_(trappedResult))

PRI testT0_7() | trappedA, trappedB, trappedC
' AE: two separate isp_bldc_motor instances, testSetup() on deliberately
' overlapping pin groups -- PINS_P0_P15 and PINS_P8_P23 overlap on P8-P15, the
' audit's own example. AE is now FIXED (task #3484): validatePinBase() claims a
' shared DAT-level registry of in-use pin ranges and ABORTS on overlap (a
' deliberate choice -- two driver cogs sharing pins is a wiring hazard, not
' something to merely warn about). So motorA's testSetup() is expected to
' succeed and claim P0-P15, and motorB's is expected to ABORT (its own
' "! ERROR: validatePinBase() ..." line appears right after this test's
' "begin" tag) because P8-P23 overlaps what motorA already holds. No real
' board is wired to either base, so this only ever toggles unused pins briefly
' while probing for a board that is not there. Both testSetup() calls are
' \-trapped anyway, same as every other testSetup()/start() call in this
' harness, since they still reach confgurePowerLimits() (via init()), which
' can also abort on an illegal user.DRIVE_VOLTAGE / user.MOTOR_TYPE pairing.
'
' T0-14a/T0-14b release motorA/motorB's claims made here (P0_P15, P32_P47)
' before they run, so this test's claims never leak into theirs.
'
' @local trappedA - motorA.testSetup()'s trapped return value (expect success)
' @local trappedB - motorB.testSetup()'s trapped return value (expect a
'                    trapped abort -- the overlap AE now rejects)
' @local trappedC - motorB retried on a NON-overlapping base (expect success)

    debug("T0-7,begin,left_base,P0_P15,right_base,P8_P23")
    trappedA := \motorA.testSetup(motorA.PINS_P0_P15, user.DRIVE_VOLTAGE, motorA.BRD_AUTO_DET)
    trappedB := \motorB.testSetup(motorB.PINS_P8_P23, user.DRIVE_VOLTAGE, motorB.BRD_AUTO_DET)
    debug("T0-7,end,harness_survived,TRUE,trapped_a,", sdec_(trappedA), ",trapped_b,", sdec_(trappedB))

    ' AE's other half, and the one that matters to shipped code: two motors on
    ' NON-overlapping ranges must STILL BOTH INITIALISE. AE is the only fix in
    ' this batch able to break a working setup, and every two-wheel platform is
    ' exactly this case -- without this check nothing in Tier 0 would notice if
    ' the overlap test started rejecting legitimate configurations. motorA still
    ' holds P0_P15 from above; P32_P47 neither overlaps it nor is held by the
    ' main `motor` instance (which holds T0_MOTOR_BASE from T0-1 onward).
    debug("T0-7,nonoverlap,begin,held_base,P0_P15,new_base,P32_P47")
    trappedC := \motorB.testSetup(motorB.PINS_P32_P47, user.DRIVE_VOLTAGE, motorB.BRD_AUTO_DET)
    debug("T0-7,nonoverlap,end,trapped_c,", sdec_(trappedC), ",note,no_ERROR_line_above_means_both_motors_coexist")

PRI spread5(pArr) : spreadVal | idx, mx, mn
' Helper for R8-T0-ZXS (T0-11): max - min of 5 LONGs at {pArr}.
'
' @param pArr - address of a 5-element LONG array
' @returns spreadVal - max(pArr[0..4]) - min(pArr[0..4])
' @local idx - loop index
' @local mx - running maximum
' @local mn - running minimum

    mx := LONG[pArr][0]
    mn := LONG[pArr][0]
    repeat idx from 1 to 4
        if LONG[pArr][idx] > mx
            mx := LONG[pArr][idx]
        if LONG[pArr][idx] < mn
            mn := LONG[pArr][idx]
    spreadVal := mx - mn

PRI emitZxsSignoff(pCritStr, measuredSpread, validCount, bAborted)
' Helper for R8-T0-ZXS (T0-11): emit one channel's SIGNOFF record. n,0/NOMEAS
' when any of T0-11's start()s aborted (design SS H.1 -- every channel instance
' stands on all five starts, so an abort makes all four NOMEAS); otherwise
' NOMEAS with n = validCount when fewer than 5 valid lifetimes were captured
' (design SS A.5-e/H.1); the 5-of-5 path prints measuredSpread against
' SF_ZXS_LO..SF_ZXS_HI.
'
' Worst-case bytes for this line ("R8-T0-ZXS"/"ZXS_I".."ZXS_W", motor RIGHT,
' measured up to -2_147_483_648, n 5, verdict FAIL): counted by hand at 130
' bytes, well under the 255-byte per-debug() limit (test_bench_detect.spin2
' header) and under design SS B.2's general 193-byte bound.
'
' @param pCritStr - pointer to "ZXS_I"/"ZXS_U"/"ZXS_V"/"ZXS_W"
' @param measuredSpread - spread5()'s result for this channel (ignored, NA, when validCount < 5)
' @param validCount - number of valid lifetimes captured (0..5)
' @param bAborted - TRUE when any of T0-11's start()s aborted

    if bAborted
        debug("SIGNOFF,sf,1,bin,T0,cell,R8-T0-ZXS,task,3529,motor,RIGHT,crit,", zstr_(pCritStr), ",measured,NA,lo,", sdec_(SF_ZXS_LO), ",hi,", sdec_(SF_ZXS_HI), ",units,MV_X10,n,0,verdict,NOMEAS")
    elseif validCount == 5
        debug("SIGNOFF,sf,1,bin,T0,cell,R8-T0-ZXS,task,3529,motor,RIGHT,crit,", zstr_(pCritStr), ",measured,", sdec_(measuredSpread), ",lo,", sdec_(SF_ZXS_LO), ",hi,", sdec_(SF_ZXS_HI), ",units,MV_X10,n,5,verdict,", zstr_(((measuredSpread >= SF_ZXS_LO) and (measuredSpread <= SF_ZXS_HI)) ? @"PASS" : @"FAIL"))
    else
        debug("SIGNOFF,sf,1,bin,T0,cell,R8-T0-ZXS,task,3529,motor,RIGHT,crit,", zstr_(pCritStr), ",measured,NA,lo,", sdec_(SF_ZXS_LO), ",hi,", sdec_(SF_ZXS_HI), ",units,MV_X10,n,", udec_(validCount), ",verdict,NOMEAS")

PRI testT0_11() | cycleIdx, validCount, startResult, bAborted, bAnyAborted, readyMs, sampleIdx, sumI, sumU, sumV, sumW, meanI[5], meanU[5], meanV[5], meanW[5], nDuty, nErr, nSenseI, nSenseU, nSenseV, nSenseW, eDrvrState, bDidFault, bValid, spreadI, spreadU, spreadV, spreadW
' R8-T0-ZXS (task 3529), design SS H.1: 5 cycles of start() -> wait ready
' (<= 2000 ms, T0 has no watchdog) -> 200 samples x 5 ms of testGetTelemetry()
' i/u/v/w at zero command (start() leaves the command at zero, drive floated)
' -> stop() -> 500 ms rest. Per channel: max - min of the 5 lifetime means
' (in mV x10) is the measured value; fewer than 5 valid lifetimes is NOMEAS.
'
' PL-21: telemetry is read only while `motor`'s own driver cog is actually
' running (start() succeeded AND isReady() went TRUE within the 2000 ms
' budget) -- otherwise this cycle contributes no lifetime at all, exactly
' the frozen-telemetry hazard PL-21 documents.
'
' Accumulator bound: sense_*_mV is a millivolt reading against the driver's
' 3300 mV ADC scale (isp_bldc_motor.spin2:2617, numerator = 3300 mV << 11),
' so |sense_x_mV| <= 5000 with generous margin. Over 200 samples,
' |sumX| <= 200 * 5000 = 1_000_000, and |sumX * 10| <= 10_000_000 -- both
' comfortably inside the 32-bit signed range (+-2_147_483_647).
'
' Abort (design SS H.1): each start() goes through startTrapped(); an aborted
' start() yields 0, which `startResult >= 0` alone would accept as a cog id, so
' a cycle whose start() aborted is never valid, and if ANY cycle's start()
' aborted all four channel records are NOMEAS,n,0 (see VAR { abort-trap
' completion flag }). The T0-11 skipped and end lines say whether it did.
'
' @local cycleIdx - 0..4, which of the 5 start()/stop() cycles
' @local validCount - number of cycles that produced a valid lifetime (0..5)
' @local startResult - \-trapped start() return for this cycle
' @local bAborted - TRUE only when this cycle's start() aborted
' @local bAnyAborted - TRUE when any cycle's start() aborted
' @local readyMs - ready-wait accumulator, bounded at 2000 ms
' @local sampleIdx - 0..199, which telemetry sample within a lifetime
' @local sumI/sumU/sumV/sumW - per-lifetime accumulators (see bound above)
' @local meanI/meanU/meanV/meanW - the up-to-5 lifetime means, in mV x10
' @local nDuty/nErr/nSenseI/nSenseU/nSenseV/nSenseW/eDrvrState/bDidFault - testGetTelemetry()'s full return tuple
' @local bValid - TRUE when this cycle's start() succeeded and went ready in time
' @local spreadI/spreadU/spreadV/spreadW - spread5()'s result per channel (NA when validCount < 5)

    debug("T0-11,begin")
    validCount := 0
    bAnyAborted := FALSE
    repeat cycleIdx from 0 to 4
        startResult, bAborted := startTrapped()
        if bAborted
            bAnyAborted := TRUE
        readyMs := 0
        repeat while (motor.isReady() == FALSE) and (readyMs < 2000)
            waitms(10)
            readyMs += 10
        bValid := (bAborted == FALSE) and (startResult >= 0) and motor.isReady()
        if bValid
            sumI := 0
            sumU := 0
            sumV := 0
            sumW := 0
            repeat sampleIdx from 0 to 199
                nDuty, nErr, nSenseI, nSenseU, nSenseV, nSenseW, eDrvrState, bDidFault := motor.testGetTelemetry()
                sumI += nSenseI
                sumU += nSenseU
                sumV += nSenseV
                sumW += nSenseW
                waitms(5)
            meanI[validCount] := (sumI * 10) / 200
            meanU[validCount] := (sumU * 10) / 200
            meanV[validCount] := (sumV * 10) / 200
            meanW[validCount] := (sumW * 10) / 200
            debug("T0-11,lifetime,", udec_(validCount), ",mean_i_x10,", sdec_(meanI[validCount]), ",mean_u_x10,", sdec_(meanU[validCount]), ",mean_v_x10,", sdec_(meanV[validCount]), ",mean_w_x10,", sdec_(meanW[validCount]))
            validCount += 1
        else
            debug("T0-11,cycle,", udec_(cycleIdx), ",skipped,not_ready,start_result,", sdec_(startResult), ",aborted,", zstr_(bAborted ? @"TRUE" : @"FALSE"))
        motor.stop()
        waitms(500)

    if validCount == 5
        spreadI := spread5(@meanI)
        spreadU := spread5(@meanU)
        spreadV := spread5(@meanV)
        spreadW := spread5(@meanW)
    debug("T0-11,end,valid_lifetimes,", udec_(validCount), ",aborted,", zstr_(bAnyAborted ? @"TRUE" : @"FALSE"))
    emitZxsSignoff(@"ZXS_I", spreadI, validCount, bAnyAborted)
    emitZxsSignoff(@"ZXS_U", spreadU, validCount, bAnyAborted)
    emitZxsSignoff(@"ZXS_V", spreadV, validCount, bAnyAborted)
    emitZxsSignoff(@"ZXS_W", spreadW, validCount, bAnyAborted)

PRI testT0_13() | startResult, bAborted, readyMs, missedCount, illegalCount, sumCounts, bReady, bPass
' R3-T0-STOPPED (task 3501), design SS H.1: start at zero command, wait ready
' (<= 2000 ms), hold 1000 ms, read both hall integrity counts. measured =
' missed + illegal; a stationary motor's hall code never transitions, so the
' criterion is exactly 0.
' Abort (design SS H.1): start() goes through startTrapped(), and the abort check
' comes before the ready check -- an aborted start() yields 0, which
' `startResult >= 0` alone would accept as a cog id. An abort prints NOMEAS,n,0
' (see VAR { abort-trap completion flag }); the T0-13 end line says whether it did.
'
' @local startResult - \-trapped start() return
' @local bAborted - TRUE only when start() aborted
' @local readyMs - ready-wait accumulator, bounded at 2000 ms
' @local missedCount - getHallIntegrityCounts()'s nMissedTransitions
' @local illegalCount - getHallIntegrityCounts()'s nIllegalCodes
' @local sumCounts - missedCount + illegalCount, this cell's measured value
' @local bReady - TRUE when the driver reached ready within budget
' @local bPass - this cell's verdict

    debug("T0-13,begin")
    startResult, bAborted := startTrapped()
    readyMs := 0
    repeat while (motor.isReady() == FALSE) and (readyMs < 2000)
        waitms(10)
        readyMs += 10
    bReady := motor.isReady()
    if bAborted
        debug("T0-13,end,start_aborted,start_result,", sdec_(startResult), ",aborted,TRUE")
        debug("SIGNOFF,sf,1,bin,T0,cell,R3-T0-STOPPED,task,3501,motor,NONE,crit,STOPPED_COUNTS,measured,NA,lo,", sdec_(SF_STOP_LO), ",hi,", sdec_(SF_STOP_HI), ",units,COUNT,n,0,verdict,NOMEAS")
    elseif (startResult >= 0) and bReady
        waitms(1000)
        missedCount, illegalCount := motor.getHallIntegrityCounts()
        sumCounts := missedCount + illegalCount
        bPass := (sumCounts == SF_STOP_LO)
        debug("T0-13,end,missed,", udec_(missedCount), ",illegal,", udec_(illegalCount), ",aborted,FALSE")
        debug("SIGNOFF,sf,1,bin,T0,cell,R3-T0-STOPPED,task,3501,motor,NONE,crit,STOPPED_COUNTS,measured,", sdec_(sumCounts), ",lo,", sdec_(SF_STOP_LO), ",hi,", sdec_(SF_STOP_HI), ",units,COUNT,n,1,verdict,", zstr_(bPass ? @"PASS" : @"FAIL"))
    else
        debug("T0-13,end,not_ready,start_result,", sdec_(startResult), ",aborted,FALSE")
        debug("SIGNOFF,sf,1,bin,T0,cell,R3-T0-STOPPED,task,3501,motor,NONE,crit,STOPPED_COUNTS,measured,NA,lo,", sdec_(SF_STOP_LO), ",hi,", sdec_(SF_STOP_HI), ",units,COUNT,n,0,verdict,NOMEAS")
    motor.stop()

PRI testT0_14a() | baseIdx, pinBase, iter, bSetupAborted, bBaseAborted, eBoardRev, notRevBCount, pMotorTok
' R2-T0-REPEAT (task 3500), design SS H.1: 32 x testSetup() + getBoardType()
' on each populated base, P16 and P32. motorA/motorB are stopped first so
' T0-7's pin claims are released before this test claims the same bases.
' Abort (design SS H.1): each testSetup() goes through setupTrapped(). One that
' aborted in validatePinBase() (isp_bldc_motor.spin2:259) holds no claim, so the
' getBoardType() after it reads REV_Unknown without touching a pin (:893) -- a
' read of nothing. A base with ANY of its 32 testSetup()s aborted is NOMEAS,n,0
' for that base's record (see VAR { abort-trap completion flag }); the T0-14a
' line says whether it was.
'
' @local baseIdx - 0 (T0_MOTOR_BASE) or 1 (T0_SECOND_BASE)
' @local pinBase - the base under test this iteration
' @local iter - 0..31, which of the 32 reads
' @local bSetupAborted - TRUE only when this read's testSetup() aborted
' @local bBaseAborted - TRUE when any of this base's 32 testSetup()s aborted
' @local eBoardRev - getBoardType()'s return for this read
' @local notRevBCount - this base's measured value: reads that were not REV_B
' @local pMotorTok - "RIGHT" for P16, "LEFT" for P32 (the bench boards), the record's motor field

    debug("T0-14,begin,repeat")
    motorA.stop()
    motorB.stop()

    repeat baseIdx from 0 to 1
        if baseIdx == 0
            pinBase := T0_MOTOR_BASE
            pMotorTok := @"RIGHT"
        else
            pinBase := T0_SECOND_BASE
            pMotorTok := @"LEFT"
        notRevBCount := 0
        bBaseAborted := FALSE
        repeat iter from 0 to 31
            bSetupAborted := setupTrapped(pinBase)
            if bSetupAborted
                bBaseAborted := TRUE
            eBoardRev := motor.getBoardType()
            if eBoardRev <> motor.REV_B
                notRevBCount += 1
        debug("T0-14a,base,", udec_(pinBase), ",not_revb_count,", udec_(notRevBCount), ",aborted,", zstr_(bBaseAborted ? @"TRUE" : @"FALSE"))
        if bBaseAborted
            debug("SIGNOFF,sf,1,bin,T0,cell,R2-T0-REPEAT,task,3500,motor,", zstr_(pMotorTok), ",crit,READS_NOT_REVB,measured,NA,lo,", sdec_(SF_REPEAT_LO), ",hi,", sdec_(SF_REPEAT_HI), ",units,COUNT,n,0,verdict,NOMEAS")
        else
            debug("SIGNOFF,sf,1,bin,T0,cell,R2-T0-REPEAT,task,3500,motor,", zstr_(pMotorTok), ",crit,READS_NOT_REVB,measured,", sdec_(notRevBCount), ",lo,", sdec_(SF_REPEAT_LO), ",hi,", sdec_(SF_REPEAT_HI), ",units,COUNT,n,32,verdict,", zstr_((notRevBCount == 0) ? @"PASS" : @"FAIL"))
    motor.stop()

PRI testT0_14b() | baseIdx, pinBase, otherBase, deadGap, pwmLimit, dutyMin, dutyMax, adcFrame, frameCnt, pinAdcX, eBoardRev, bSetupAborted, startResult, readyMs, bDirtyIsRevB, pMotorTok
' R2-T0-DIRTY (task 3500), design SS H.1: on each populated base, an
' initialised but NOT running group. The harness itself drives base+4 into
' the driver's own steady-state ADC sampling mode -- adc_modes+2 =
' p_adc_1x | p_count_highs, WRPIN'd onto adc_pins at isp_bldc_motor.spin2:2913
' (mode constants at :2633..2635); the matching count period is adc_fram,
' WXPIN'd at :2909, and this test reads adc_fram back through the existing
' testGetDriveConstants() getter rather than recomputing it -- then leaves
' the pin with DIR low (pinfloat(), which per spin2-authoring-guide.md:1270
' clears DIR only and leaves the WRPIN mode set), exactly the state an idle
' driver cog would
' leave it in without the "defensive clear" getBoardType() performs (its own
' pinclear() at :900 when motorCog == 0). measured TRUE when the read that
' follows is REV_B; this is the cell that FAILs if that defensive clear ever
' regresses.
'
' Also: start() -> ready -> stop() on the same group, then start the OTHER
' group on motorA in between (to confirm it stays clean of this group's
' state), then testSetup()+getBoardType() again on the original group.
' Printed as T0-14b CSV lines; not a separate sign-off instance (design
' SS H.1 states one SIGNOFF per base for this cell).
'
' Abort (design SS H.1): the verdict stands on the first testSetup(), which goes
' through setupTrapped(). One that aborted in validatePinBase()
' (isp_bldc_motor.spin2:259) holds no claim, so the dirty-pin getBoardType() reads
' REV_Unknown without touching a pin (:893) -- a read of nothing. That base's
' record is then NOMEAS,n,0 (see VAR { abort-trap completion flag }); the
' dirty_read line says whether it was. The confirm cycle's start()s and second
' testSetup() only feed the printed poststart_read, never the verdict, so they
' stay plainly \-trapped.
'
' @local baseIdx - 0 (T0_MOTOR_BASE) or 1 (T0_SECOND_BASE)
' @local pinBase - the base under test this iteration
' @local otherBase - the other populated base, started on motorA in between
' @local deadGap/pwmLimit/dutyMin/dutyMax/adcFrame/frameCnt - testGetDriveConstants()'s full return tuple (only adcFrame used)
' @local pinAdcX - pinBase + 4, the detection/ADC-common pin
' @local eBoardRev - getBoardType()'s return, read twice per base
' @local bSetupAborted - TRUE only when the first testSetup() on this base aborted
' @local startResult - \-trapped start() return for the confirm cycle
' @local readyMs - ready-wait accumulator, bounded at 2000 ms, reused for both confirm starts
' @local bDirtyIsRevB - this base's measured value: the dirty-pin read was REV_B
' @local pMotorTok - "RIGHT" for P16, "LEFT" for P32 (the bench boards), the record's motor field

    debug("T0-14,begin,dirty")
    motorA.stop()
    motorB.stop()

    repeat baseIdx from 0 to 1
        if baseIdx == 0
            pinBase := T0_MOTOR_BASE
            otherBase := T0_SECOND_BASE
            pMotorTok := @"RIGHT"
        else
            pinBase := T0_SECOND_BASE
            otherBase := T0_MOTOR_BASE
            pMotorTok := @"LEFT"

        bSetupAborted := setupTrapped(pinBase)
        deadGap, pwmLimit, dutyMin, dutyMax, adcFrame, frameCnt := motor.testGetDriveConstants()
        pinAdcX := pinBase + 4

        wrpin(pinAdcX, P_ADC_1X | P_COUNT_HIGHS)
        wxpin(pinAdcX, adcFrame)
        pinfloat(pinAdcX)                              ' DIR low; PINFLOAT() clears DIR only, the WRPIN mode survives (spin2-authoring-guide.md:1270)

        eBoardRev := motor.getBoardType()
        bDirtyIsRevB := (eBoardRev == motor.REV_B)
        debug("T0-14b,base,", udec_(pinBase), ",dirty_read,", udec_(eBoardRev), ",aborted,", zstr_(bSetupAborted ? @"TRUE" : @"FALSE"))

        startResult := \motor.start(pinBase, user.DRIVE_VOLTAGE, motor.BRD_AUTO_DET)
        readyMs := 0
        repeat while (motor.isReady() == FALSE) and (readyMs < 2000)
            waitms(10)
            readyMs += 10
        motor.stop()

        \motorA.start(otherBase, user.DRIVE_VOLTAGE, motorA.BRD_AUTO_DET)
        readyMs := 0
        repeat while (motorA.isReady() == FALSE) and (readyMs < 2000)
            waitms(10)
            readyMs += 10
        motorA.stop()

        \motor.testSetup(pinBase, user.DRIVE_VOLTAGE, motor.BRD_AUTO_DET)
        eBoardRev := motor.getBoardType()
        debug("T0-14b,base,", udec_(pinBase), ",poststart_read,", udec_(eBoardRev))

        if bSetupAborted
            debug("SIGNOFF,sf,1,bin,T0,cell,R2-T0-DIRTY,task,3500,motor,", zstr_(pMotorTok), ",crit,POSTSTOP_REVB,measured,NA,lo,TRUE,hi,TRUE,units,BOOL,n,0,verdict,NOMEAS")
        else
            debug("SIGNOFF,sf,1,bin,T0,cell,R2-T0-DIRTY,task,3500,motor,", zstr_(pMotorTok), ",crit,POSTSTOP_REVB,measured,", zstr_(bDirtyIsRevB ? @"TRUE" : @"FALSE"), ",lo,TRUE,hi,TRUE,units,BOOL,n,1,verdict,", zstr_(bDirtyIsRevB ? @"PASS" : @"FAIL"))
    motor.stop()

PRI testT0_14c() | bSetupAborted, eBoardRev, bEmpty
' R2-T0-EMPTY (task 3500), design SS H.1: testSetup(PINS_P0_P15) +
' getBoardType(). measured TRUE when it reads REV_Unknown. NEVER probe
' PINS_P40_P55: its sense pin P44 is the LEFT board's pin_pwm_w_l (32 + 12),
' and T0 runs with the rail on -- getBoardType() drives it high for 1 ms
' (isp_bldc_motor.spin2:889-890, hazard also recorded at
' test_bench_detect.spin2:161-165).
' Abort (design SS H.1): testSetup() goes through setupTrapped(). One that aborted
' in validatePinBase() (isp_bldc_motor.spin2:259) holds no claim, so getBoardType()
' returns REV_Unknown without touching a pin (:893) -- exactly this cell's PASS
' value, measured from nothing. An abort prints NOMEAS,n,0 instead (see
' VAR { abort-trap completion flag }); the T0-14c line says whether it did.
'
' @local bSetupAborted - TRUE only when testSetup() aborted
' @local eBoardRev - getBoardType()'s return
' @local bEmpty - this cell's measured value: the read was REV_Unknown

    debug("T0-14,begin,empty")
    bSetupAborted := setupTrapped(motor.PINS_P0_P15)
    eBoardRev := motor.getBoardType()
    bEmpty := (eBoardRev == motor.REV_Unknown)
    debug("T0-14c,base,P0_P15,read,", udec_(eBoardRev), ",aborted,", zstr_(bSetupAborted ? @"TRUE" : @"FALSE"))
    if bSetupAborted
        debug("SIGNOFF,sf,1,bin,T0,cell,R2-T0-EMPTY,task,3500,motor,NONE,crit,EMPTY_NODET,measured,NA,lo,TRUE,hi,TRUE,units,BOOL,n,0,verdict,NOMEAS")
    else
        debug("SIGNOFF,sf,1,bin,T0,cell,R2-T0-EMPTY,task,3500,motor,NONE,crit,EMPTY_NODET,measured,", zstr_(bEmpty ? @"TRUE" : @"FALSE"), ",lo,TRUE,hi,TRUE,units,BOOL,n,1,verdict,", zstr_(bEmpty ? @"PASS" : @"FAIL"))
    motor.stop()

PRI countFreeCogs() : freeCount | idx, spareCogId, spareId[MAX_SPACER_COGS]
' Shared helper for T0-15: count free cogs the SS A.5-a way -- start spacer
' cogs with cogspin() until one returns < 0 (not == -1: the library documents
' the $8000_xxxx exhaustion form), record the count, then stop them all.
' Reuses the T0-8/T0-15 spacerStacks buffer; safe because every caller of
' this helper (and T0-8 itself) runs strictly sequentially, never overlapping
' in time with another cog-exhaustion probe.
'
' @returns freeCount - number of cogs that could be started just now
' @local idx - loop index
' @local spareCogId - cogspin()'s return for the current spacer attempt
' @local spareId - cog ids of the spacers this call started, so they can be stopped

    freeCount := 0
    repeat idx from 0 to MAX_SPACER_COGS - 1
        spareCogId := cogspin(NEWCOG, spacerLoop(), @spacerStacks[idx * SPACER_STACK_LONGS])
        if spareCogId < 0
            quit
        spareId[freeCount] := spareCogId
        freeCount += 1
    repeat idx from 0 to freeCount - 1
        cogstop(spareId[idx])

PRI testT0_15a() | startResult, bAborted, rawMotorCog, bPass
' R1-T0-START (task 3499), design SS H.1: start() on P16. The return must be
' in 0..7 and equal testGetMotorCog() - 1. A BOOL cell (task 3537): measured is
' TRUE only when both hold; the two raw numbers are on the T0-15a line.
' NOMEAS,n,0 when start() aborted, found by startTrapped()'s completion flag
' (see VAR { abort-trap completion flag }); the T0-15a line says whether it did.
'
' @local startResult - \-trapped start() return
' @local bAborted - TRUE only when start() aborted
' @local rawMotorCog - testGetMotorCog()'s snapshot, taken right after start()
' @local bPass - this cell's measured value and verdict

    debug("T0-15,begin,start")
    startResult, bAborted := startTrapped()
    rawMotorCog := motor.testGetMotorCog()
    bPass := (startResult >= SF_COG_LO) and (startResult <= SF_COG_HI) and (startResult == rawMotorCog - 1)
    debug("T0-15a,start_return,", sdec_(startResult), ",raw_motor_cog,", sdec_(rawMotorCog), ",aborted,", zstr_(bAborted ? @"TRUE" : @"FALSE"))
    if bAborted
        debug("SIGNOFF,sf,1,bin,T0,cell,R1-T0-START,task,3499,motor,NONE,crit,RET_EQ_COG_M1,measured,NA,lo,TRUE,hi,TRUE,units,BOOL,n,0,verdict,NOMEAS")
    else
        debug("SIGNOFF,sf,1,bin,T0,cell,R1-T0-START,task,3499,motor,NONE,crit,RET_EQ_COG_M1,measured,", zstr_(bPass ? @"TRUE" : @"FALSE"), ",lo,TRUE,hi,TRUE,units,BOOL,n,1,verdict,", zstr_(bPass ? @"PASS" : @"FAIL"))
    motor.stop()

PRI testT0_15c() | baseline, startResult1, bAbort1, free1, startResult2, bAbort2, free2, free3, diffFree, bPass
' R1-T0-RESTART (task 3499), design SS H.1: count free cogs (baseline) ->
' start() -> free1 -> start() again with NO stop() -> free2 -> stop() ->
' free3. A BOOL cell (task 3537): measured is TRUE only when
' |free2 - free1| + |free3 - baseline| == 0 AND free1 == baseline - 1 (PL-24:
' a second start() must not orphan the first cog); the four free-cog counts
' are on the T0-15c line. T0-15d reads state immediately after this test's own stop(), so it
' must be called right after this one from main().
' The cell judges both start()s, so it is NOMEAS,n,0 when EITHER aborted, found by
' startTrapped()'s completion flag (see VAR { abort-trap completion flag }); the
' T0-15c line says whether each did.
'
' @local baseline - free cogs before either start()
' @local startResult1 - \-trapped first start() return
' @local bAbort1 - TRUE only when the first start() aborted
' @local free1 - free cogs after the first start()
' @local startResult2 - \-trapped second start() return, no intervening stop()
' @local bAbort2 - TRUE only when the second start() aborted
' @local free2 - free cogs after the second start()
' @local free3 - free cogs after this test's stop()
' @local diffFree - abs(free2-free1) + abs(free3-baseline), one of this cell's two conditions
' @local bPass - this cell's measured value and verdict

    debug("T0-15,begin,restart")
    bRestartStopValid := FALSE
    baseline := countFreeCogs()
    startResult1, bAbort1 := startTrapped()
    free1 := countFreeCogs()
    startResult2, bAbort2 := startTrapped()
    free2 := countFreeCogs()
    motor.stop()
    bRestartStopValid := (bAbort1 == FALSE) and (bAbort2 == FALSE) and (startResult1 >= 0) and (startResult2 >= 0)
    free3 := countFreeCogs()
    diffFree := abs(free2 - free1) + abs(free3 - baseline)
    bPass := (diffFree == SF_RESTART_LO) and (free1 == baseline - 1)
    debug("T0-15c,baseline,", udec_(baseline), ",free1,", udec_(free1), ",start1,", sdec_(startResult1), ",free2,", udec_(free2), ",start2,", sdec_(startResult2), ",free3,", udec_(free3), ",aborted1,", zstr_(bAbort1 ? @"TRUE" : @"FALSE"), ",aborted2,", zstr_(bAbort2 ? @"TRUE" : @"FALSE"))
    if bAbort1 or bAbort2
        debug("SIGNOFF,sf,1,bin,T0,cell,R1-T0-RESTART,task,3499,motor,NONE,crit,NO_ORPHAN,measured,NA,lo,TRUE,hi,TRUE,units,BOOL,n,0,verdict,NOMEAS")
    else
        debug("SIGNOFF,sf,1,bin,T0,cell,R1-T0-RESTART,task,3499,motor,NONE,crit,NO_ORPHAN,measured,", zstr_(bPass ? @"TRUE" : @"FALSE"), ",lo,TRUE,hi,TRUE,units,BOOL,n,1,verdict,", zstr_(bPass ? @"PASS" : @"FAIL"))

PRI testT0_15d() | bReady, bStopped, eState, bPass
' R10-T0-STOPREADY (task 3533), design SS H.1: right after T0-15c's own
' stop() (this method must run immediately after testT0_15c() from main(),
' with no other call touching `motor` in between). measured TRUE when
' isReady() is FALSE AND isStopped() is FALSE (PL-28 item 2 / task 3533:
' stop() now leaves drv_state at DCS_Unknown, not stale). getDriverState()
' is logged beside the verdict; DCS_Unknown is expected.
' Abort (design SS H.1): this cell judges the state T0-15c's own stop() left, so
' it is NOMEAS,n,0 when either of T0-15c's start()s aborted or returned -1, or
' T0-15c never reached its stop() -- bRestartStopValid FALSE (see VAR { abort-trap
' completion flag }). The T0-15d line prints that as t0_15c_aborted TRUE.
'
' @local bReady - motor.isReady()'s value right now
' @local bStopped - motor.isStopped()'s value right now
' @local eState - motor.getDriverState()'s value right now (expect DCS_Unknown)
' @local bPass - this cell's verdict

    bReady := motor.isReady()
    bStopped := motor.isStopped()
    eState := motor.getDriverState()
    bPass := (bReady == FALSE) and (bStopped == FALSE)
    debug("T0-15d,driver_state,", udec_(eState), ",ready,", zstr_(bReady ? @"TRUE" : @"FALSE"), ",stopped,", zstr_(bStopped ? @"TRUE" : @"FALSE"), ",t0_15c_aborted,", zstr_(bRestartStopValid ? @"FALSE" : @"TRUE"))
    if bRestartStopValid == FALSE
        debug("SIGNOFF,sf,1,bin,T0,cell,R10-T0-STOPREADY,task,3533,motor,NONE,crit,STOP_NOT_READY,measured,NA,lo,TRUE,hi,TRUE,units,BOOL,n,0,verdict,NOMEAS")
    else
        debug("SIGNOFF,sf,1,bin,T0,cell,R10-T0-STOPREADY,task,3533,motor,NONE,crit,STOP_NOT_READY,measured,", zstr_(bPass ? @"TRUE" : @"FALSE"), ",lo,TRUE,hi,TRUE,units,BOOL,n,1,verdict,", zstr_(bPass ? @"PASS" : @"FAIL"))

PRI testT0_8() | spacerIdx, spacerCogId, spacerCount, startResult, spacerId[MAX_SPACER_COGS]
' C, AD: occupy every other cog, then call the real start() (not testSetup())
' and print its raw return. coginit() returns the documented $8000_xxxx form
' on failure (isp_bldc_motor.spin2:110-113), not a bare -1 -- the spacer-count
' loop below tests cogspin()'s own return the same way (< 0, not == -1),
' since a P2 cogspin() failure return uses the identical negative-value
' convention. start() itself still returns -1 on failure specifically
' (:116), which is what this test's SIGNOFF (R1-T0-EXHAUST, T0-15b) checks
' -- this test (T0-8) exists to occupy every cog and print the raw value, not
' to judge it; R1-T0-EXHAUST is the harsher, later probe that also confirms
' no cog leaked.
'
' T0-8 stays after every non-destructive test (T0-1..T0-7, T0-10, T0-11,
' T0-13, T0-14a/b/c, T0-15a/c/d): it occupies every spare cog so start()
' must fail, which leaves the object half-initialised. R1-T0-EXHAUST
' (T0-15b) is destructive in the same way and runs even later, after T0-8's
' own spacers have been released again -- see main()'s ordering comment.
'
' @local spacerIdx - loop index over the spacer-cog array
' @local spacerCogId - cogspin()'s return for the current spacer attempt
' @local spacerCount - number of spacer cogs actually started
' @local startResult - start()'s trapped, raw return value under cog exhaustion
'                       (start() also reaches confgurePowerLimits() via init(),
'                       so it is \-trapped like every other testSetup()/start()
'                       call in this harness; its own -1-on-failure convention
'                       already overlaps the trapped-abort-returns-0 case, so
'                       this adds no new ambiguity beyond what start()'s doc
'                       already carries)

    debug("T0-8,begin")
    spacerCount := 0
    repeat spacerIdx from 0 to MAX_SPACER_COGS - 1
        spacerCogId := cogspin(NEWCOG, spacerLoop(), @spacerStacks[spacerIdx * SPACER_STACK_LONGS])
        if spacerCogId < 0
            quit
        spacerId[spacerIdx] := spacerCogId
        spacerCount += 1

    startResult := \motor.start(T0_MOTOR_BASE, user.DRIVE_VOLTAGE, motor.BRD_AUTO_DET)
    debug("T0-8,end,cogs_occupied,", udec_(spacerCount), ",start_return,", sdec_(startResult))

    ' stop() unconditionally. A start() that returned -1 may STILL have gotten
    ' partway -- the 2026-09-10 run shows a driver cog reaching INIT on a call
    ' that reported failure -- so the object can be left half-initialised, and
    ' anything that starts it afterwards then fails too. Leave it clean.
    motor.stop()

    repeat spacerIdx from 0 to spacerCount - 1
        cogstop(spacerId[spacerIdx])

PRI spacerLoop()
' Idle forever -- exists only to occupy a cog so start() has none left (T0-8, T0-15b).
'

    repeat
        waitms(1000)

PRI startTrapped() : startResult, bAborted
' Call motor.start() on T0_MOTOR_BASE under an abort trap and report whether it
' aborted, by completion flag (see VAR { abort-trap completion flag }). For
' R8-T0-ZXS (T0-11), R3-T0-STOPPED (T0-13), R1-T0-START (T0-15a), R1-T0-RESTART
' and R10-T0-STOPREADY (T0-15c/d) and R1-T0-EXHAUST (T0-15b).
'
' @returns startResult - start()'s return: cog id 0..7 or -1, or the trap's value when bAborted
' @returns bAborted - TRUE only when start() aborted

    bTrapPending := TRUE
    startResult := \startCall()
    bAborted := bTrapPending
    bTrapPending := FALSE

PRI startCall() : startResult
' motor.start() itself; clears bTrapPending only when start() returns normally.
' Call only as \startCall() from startTrapped().
'
' @returns startResult - start()'s return

    startResult := motor.start(T0_MOTOR_BASE, user.DRIVE_VOLTAGE, motor.BRD_AUTO_DET)
    bTrapPending := FALSE

PRI setupTrapped(pinBase) : bAborted | trappedResult
' Call motor.testSetup() on {pinBase} under an abort trap and report whether it
' aborted, by completion flag (see VAR { abort-trap completion flag }). For
' R2-T0-REPEAT (T0-14a), R2-T0-DIRTY (T0-14b) and R2-T0-EMPTY (T0-14c).
'
' @param pinBase - PINS_* base passed straight to testSetup()
' @returns bAborted - TRUE only when testSetup() aborted
' @local trappedResult - the trap's value, discarded (testSetup() has no result)

    bTrapPending := TRUE
    trappedResult := \setupCall(pinBase)
    bAborted := bTrapPending
    bTrapPending := FALSE

PRI setupCall(pinBase) : callResult
' motor.testSetup() itself; clears bTrapPending only when it returns normally.
' Call only as \setupCall() from setupTrapped().
'
' @param pinBase - PINS_* base passed straight to testSetup()
' @returns callResult - always 0: testSetup() returns no value

    motor.testSetup(pinBase, user.DRIVE_VOLTAGE, motor.BRD_AUTO_DET)
    bTrapPending := FALSE
    callResult := 0

PRI stopDistanceTrapped(nDistance, eDistanceUnits) : trappedResult, bAborted
' Call motor.stopAfterDistance() under an abort trap and report whether it aborted,
' by completion flag (see VAR { abort-trap completion flag }). For R4-T0-1M-TICKS (T0-3).
'
' @param nDistance - distance passed straight to stopAfterDistance()
' @param eDistanceUnits - DDU_* units passed straight to stopAfterDistance()
' @returns trappedResult - 0 on a normal return (stopAfterDistance() has no result), or the trap's value when bAborted
' @returns bAborted - TRUE only when stopAfterDistance() aborted

    bTrapPending := TRUE
    trappedResult := \stopDistanceCall(nDistance, eDistanceUnits)
    bAborted := bTrapPending
    bTrapPending := FALSE

PRI stopDistanceCall(nDistance, eDistanceUnits) : callResult
' motor.stopAfterDistance() itself; clears bTrapPending only when it returns normally.
' Call only as \stopDistanceCall() from stopDistanceTrapped().
'
' @param nDistance - distance passed straight to stopAfterDistance()
' @param eDistanceUnits - DDU_* units passed straight to stopAfterDistance()
' @returns callResult - always 0: stopAfterDistance() returns no value

    motor.stopAfterDistance(nDistance, eDistanceUnits)
    bTrapPending := FALSE
    callResult := 0

PRI testT0_10() | startResult, rawMotorCog, pinAdcX, xNodeCounts
' C-6b: pin_adc_x_i (base+3) falls inside adc_pins, so the driver already
' samples it as a calibrated, frame-locked ADC every cycle -- it is simply
' never read. Start the REAL driver (rail must be on for this one test) so the
' fourth channel is live, then read it with RQPIN so this harness never steals
' the driver's own acknowledge on a pin the driver cog rdpin's every cycle.
' Commanded speed stays at zero (start() calls setTargetAccel(0) before the
' cog launches), so nothing turns.
'
' @local startResult - start()'s trapped return value (see T0-8's note --
'                       start() reaches confgurePowerLimits() via init() and
'                       can abort, so this call is \-trapped like every other
'                       testSetup()/start() call in this harness)
' @local rawMotorCog - AD+: testGetMotorCog()'s snapshot of the object's own motorCog,
'                       printed beside startResult so tomorrow's run can tell whether
'                       start()'s return or the chained assignment that sets motorCog is
'                       where AD+'s unreliable value comes from
' @local pinAdcX - pinbase + 3, the X-node ADC pin
' @local xNodeCounts - RQPIN()'s lower 31 bits (bit 31 is the pin's C flag)

    debug("T0-10,begin,rail_must_be_on,TRUE")
    startResult := \motor.start(T0_MOTOR_BASE, user.DRIVE_VOLTAGE, motor.BRD_AUTO_DET)
    rawMotorCog := motor.testGetMotorCog()

    ' Do NOT gate the reading on start()'s return. The 2026-09-10 bench run
    ' had the object print "* Motor COG #1" -- a driver cog genuinely running
    ' -- on a call this harness saw return 0, so gating skipped the one
    ' measurement T0-10 exists to take. Report both numbers and let the
    ' analyst judge; a test's job is to report, not to decide.
    debug("T0-10,start_return,", sdec_(startResult), ",raw_motor_cog,", sdec_(rawMotorCog), ",note,see_Motor_COG_line_above_for_whether_a_cog_actually_started")
    waitms(50)                                              ' let the driver cog reach its running, calibrated state
    pinAdcX := T0_MOTOR_BASE + 3
    xNodeCounts := RQPIN(pinAdcX) & $7FFF_FFFF
    debug("T0-10,end,pin,", udec_(pinAdcX), ",x_node_counts,", udec_(xNodeCounts))
    motor.stop()

PRI testT0_15b() | spacerIdx, spacerCogId, spacerCount, spacerId[MAX_SPACER_COGS], baseline, startResult, bAborted, rawMotorCog, freeAfter, bPass
' R1-T0-EXHAUST (task 3499), design SS H.1: runs LAST, after T0-8's slot.
' Count free cogs (baseline), occupy every free cog, call the real start(),
' release the spacers, count free cogs again. A BOOL cell (task 3537):
' measured is TRUE only when start() returns -1 AND testGetMotorCog() == 0 AND
' free cogs after release == baseline, so this test itself can never leave the
' suite short a cog; the raw numbers are on the T0-15b line.
' NOMEAS,n,0 when start() aborted, found by startTrapped()'s completion flag
' (see VAR { abort-trap completion flag }) -- start()'s normal -1 is NOT an abort
' and is still judged. The T0-15b line says whether it aborted.
'
' Deliberately its own spacer loop (not countFreeCogs(), which stops its
' spacers again immediately) -- this test needs the cogs held OCCUPIED across
' the start() attempt, then released afterward.
'
' @local spacerIdx - loop index over the spacer-cog array
' @local spacerCogId - cogspin()'s return for the current spacer attempt
' @local spacerCount - number of spacer cogs actually started (occupies every free cog)
' @local spacerId - cog ids of the spacers this test started
' @local baseline - free cogs before this test occupies any
' @local startResult - \-trapped start() return under total cog exhaustion
' @local bAborted - TRUE only when start() aborted
' @local rawMotorCog - testGetMotorCog()'s snapshot after the failed start()
' @local freeAfter - free cogs after this test releases its spacers
' @local bPass - this cell's measured value and verdict

    debug("T0-15,begin,exhaust")
    baseline := countFreeCogs()

    spacerCount := 0
    repeat spacerIdx from 0 to MAX_SPACER_COGS - 1
        spacerCogId := cogspin(NEWCOG, spacerLoop(), @spacerStacks[spacerIdx * SPACER_STACK_LONGS])
        if spacerCogId < 0
            quit
        spacerId[spacerCount] := spacerCogId
        spacerCount += 1

    startResult, bAborted := startTrapped()
    rawMotorCog := motor.testGetMotorCog()
    motor.stop()

    repeat spacerIdx from 0 to spacerCount - 1
        cogstop(spacerId[spacerIdx])

    freeAfter := countFreeCogs()
    bPass := (startResult == SF_EXHAUST_LO) and (rawMotorCog == 0) and (freeAfter == baseline)
    debug("T0-15b,cogs_occupied,", udec_(spacerCount), ",start_return,", sdec_(startResult), ",raw_motor_cog,", sdec_(rawMotorCog), ",baseline,", udec_(baseline), ",free_after,", udec_(freeAfter), ",aborted,", zstr_(bAborted ? @"TRUE" : @"FALSE"))
    if bAborted
        debug("SIGNOFF,sf,1,bin,T0,cell,R1-T0-EXHAUST,task,3499,motor,NONE,crit,RET_NEG_NOLEAK,measured,NA,lo,TRUE,hi,TRUE,units,BOOL,n,0,verdict,NOMEAS")
    else
        debug("SIGNOFF,sf,1,bin,T0,cell,R1-T0-EXHAUST,task,3499,motor,NONE,crit,RET_NEG_NOLEAK,measured,", zstr_(bPass ? @"TRUE" : @"FALSE"), ",lo,TRUE,hi,TRUE,units,BOOL,n,1,verdict,", zstr_(bPass ? @"PASS" : @"FAIL"))

#ifdef T0_HAND
PRI testT0_12() | keyCode, bArmed, hallPin, hallCode, priorCode, transitions, illegalCount, pollIdx
' T0-12, hand-rotation anchor -- SEPARABLE, compiled only under -D T0_HAND
' (its own bench-run.sh tier, t0-hand), so the unattended T0 run never waits
' on a person. The operator presses a key, turns one wheel by hand exactly N
' revolutions in ONE direction, then presses a key again. It anchors 90 hall
' transitions per revolution and 5.763 mm/tick (isp_bldc_motor.spin2 hall
' tics per rotation, and DOCs/plans/VISIT-SIGNOFF-DESIGN.md SS A.5-b). No
' sign-off cell -- this is an operator-attended reference measurement.
'
' No driver cog runs here, so the driver-maintained tick count
' (getRawHallTicks() reads the driver's pos) cannot move. This harness counts
' the transitions itself: it reads the three hall inputs (base+5..base+7)
' with pinread() every T0_12_POLL_MS. They are plain inputs -- nothing ever
' raises their DIR (task 3524) -- not smart pins, so pinread() is safe and no
' RDPIN is involved. Any change of the 3-bit code counts as one transition,
' and entering an illegal code (%000 or %111, symmetric under any bit order)
' is also counted separately. At a 1 ms poll a hand turn would need more than
' 5 revolutions per second (450 transitions per second, one every ~2.2 ms)
' before two transitions could fall between polls.
'
' UNVERIFIED (compile-checked only): the pc_key() keypress-read pattern mirrors
' test_bench_char.spin2's pollKeyEdge() ("bench" PLOT window, backtick-prefixed
' debug() call), the only precedent for reading a keypress in this codebase.
'
' @local keyCode - pc_key()'s last-read key code, 0 when none is latched
' @local bArmed - TRUE once a 0 reading has been seen (so a held key cannot register twice)
' @local hallPin - base+5, the lowest of the three hall inputs
' @local hallCode - the 3-bit hall code just read
' @local priorCode - the previous poll's 3-bit hall code
' @local transitions - hall code changes counted since the start keypress
' @local illegalCount - entries into %000 or %111 since the start keypress
' @local pollIdx - polls since the start keypress, paces the key checks and progress lines

    debug(`PLOT bench TITLE 'T0-12 hand-rotation anchor' SIZE 320 100 POS 60 80 HIDEXY UPDATE)
    debug("T0-12,begin,prompt,press_any_key_then_turn_one_wheel_exactly_N_revolutions_one_direction_then_press_any_key")

    hallPin := T0_MOTOR_BASE + T0_12_HALL_OFFSET

    bArmed := FALSE
    repeat
        debug(`bench `pc_key(@keyCode))
        if keyCode == 0
            bArmed := TRUE
        if bArmed and (keyCode <> 0)
            quit
        waitms(T0_12_KEY_WAIT_MS)

    priorCode := pinread(hallPin addpins T0_12_HALL_SPAN)
    transitions := 0
    illegalCount := 0
    pollIdx := 0
    debug("T0-12,started,hall_pin,", udec_(hallPin), ",hall_code,", udec_(priorCode), ",prompt,press_any_key_to_stop_count")

    bArmed := FALSE
    repeat
        hallCode := pinread(hallPin addpins T0_12_HALL_SPAN)
        if hallCode <> priorCode
            transitions += 1
            if (hallCode == %000) or (hallCode == %111)
                illegalCount += 1
            priorCode := hallCode
        pollIdx += 1
        if (pollIdx +// T0_12_KEY_POLLS) == 0
            debug(`bench `pc_key(@keyCode))
            if keyCode == 0
                bArmed := TRUE
            if bArmed and (keyCode <> 0)
                quit
        if (pollIdx +// T0_12_PRINT_POLLS) == 0
            debug("T0-12,running,transitions,", udec_(transitions), ",illegal,", udec_(illegalCount))
        waitms(T0_12_POLL_MS)

    debug("T0-12,end,transitions,", udec_(transitions), ",illegal,", udec_(illegalCount), ",note,expect_90_per_revolution_(5.763_mm_per_tick)")
#endif

